# SB8 (PRE-WINDOW, no card opened, production keeps serving): build the SHIPPING base image tp4-serve-8 from this branch: the eight-seat traffic
# profile c2-packed-tp4-8 baked in as the image's serving default and THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP baked as that profile's max-num-seqs (computed by the
# build script from the context's own profiles file). C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE is the one key that does it: a build without it (every other tag,
# production's included) bakes nothing and its default stays qwen_c2_profiles.json's c2-packed-tp4.
# Why the image: the node agent forwards neither QWEN_C2_PROFILE nor the session cap, so what a platform launch serves is the image's own default, and
# the image is the unit of rollback (moving :latest back restores both the four-seat profile and the cap of four).
# READ: the build log's provenance report: '(c) the image default is the BAKED profile c2-packed-tp4-8', no problem line, and 'baking the serving
# default c2-packed-tp4-8 with a session cap of 8'; the build prints the image id. The build step exits early if the tag already exists (so a changed
# commit needs a new tag). Never run it during a timing job: the build loads the host (a busy host skews timed phases 10 to 20%).
# After it: the base is pushed to the registry through the platform's publish lane, the thin layer is built on it and pre-pulled (the driver's steps,
# ORDER.txt). Nothing is served here.
# Duration (estimate): 30-60 min (most layers cached from the request-warm image). Stop rule: a build or provenance failure stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8 SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8 is the SHIPPING image: the base SB8 builds
# from this branch with the eight-seat profile baked in as its serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its
# seat count (ENV THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP). Every job serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still
# names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default. A commit that changes a file the image carries needs a new SB8 build and a
# new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8
C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8
